          },
          "mechanism": "Household income affects family planning decisions (pregnancy count) and healthcare access and medication adherence.",
          "justification": "SES is a well-established confounder of both reproductive and cardiovascular outcomes.",
          "role": "confounder",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        },
        {
          "variable": {
            "kind": "variable",
            "key": "m2:Q5.6",
            "quoted_wording": "sha256:55600e24b14333ff4c2cea0d744d84df721ba906ace8329551ba8072ef427427"
          },
          "mechanism": "Type 2 Diabetes increases hypertension risk and complications, requiring more intensive antihypertensive therapy. Diabetes is not caused by pregnancy count.",
          "justification": "Diabetes is a strong risk factor for hypertension severity and medication needs independent of pregnancy history.",
          "role": "confounder",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        },
        {
          "variable": {
            "kind": "variable",
            "key": "m2:Q5.4",
            "quoted_wording": "sha256:06f26b3aeabb79ed39bb2db875106fa6274622a3256efef6a48f1c1f55525305"
          },
          "mechanism": "Type 1 Diabetes increases cardiovascular and hypertensive complications requiring more medication.",
          "justification": "Strong independent cause of hypertension medication intensity.",
          "role": "confounder",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        },
        {
          "variable": {
            "kind": "variable",
            "key": "m2:Q5.29",
            "quoted_wording": "sha256:8f7a250aae8614d933f3f746e3bda5faa34a21b8ce5e39d693311dbca6b57abc"
          },
          "mechanism": "Chronic kidney disease causes hypertension and reduces medication options, requiring more intensive therapy regardless of pregnancy history.",
          "justification": "CKD is a direct cause of hypertension and medication burden.",
          "role": "confounder",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        }
      ],
      "excluded_variables": [
        {
          "variable": {
            "kind": "variable",
            "key": "m2:Q5.8",
            "quoted_wording": "sha256:54859c0b47368445f04b396a67b96ed6934dcd16cef08c3db16e3357147c596b"
          },
          "mechanism": "The causal pathway is: pregnancy history → hypertension risk (through gestational hypertension, long-term BP elevation, weight gain) → hypertension diagnosis → antihypertensive medication need → medication intensity.",
          "justification": "Hypertension diagnosis is a mediator of the exposure-outcome relationship. Conditioning on it would estimate the direct effect of pregnancy holding constant hypertension status, which is not the estimand of interest. We seek the total effect.",
          "role": "mediator",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        },
        {
          "variable": {
            "kind": "variable",
            "key": "m2:Q9.8",
            "quoted_wording": "sha256:75280df2ed2c4c3e0d15aa33e12b34dc78154bcfe0cb34cc8a4eef4e64c7ece4"
          },
          "mechanism": "Gestational diabetes occurs as a direct consequence of being pregnant.",
          "justification": "This is a descendant of the exposure (number of pregnancies). It is not a confounder and should not be adjusted for.",
          "role": "descendant_of_exposure",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        },
        {
          "variable": {
            "kind": "variable",
            "key": "m1:Q2.10",
            "quoted_wording": "sha256:b188718a8d8144f5fe4cf3c35a60b74088dcd97a8cf89ca2f1fec01a9af8139b"
          },
          "mechanism": "Pregnancy causes weight gain; obesity causes hypertension and increases cardiovascular risk; obesity increases antihypertensive medication burden.",
          "justification": "Current weight is a mediator in the pathway from pregnancy to hypertension and medication intensity. If pregnancy increases future weight and weight increases medication intensity, weight is in the causal pathway and should be excluded to preserve the total effect.",
          "role": "mediator",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        },
        {
          "variable": {
            "kind": "variable",
            "key": "m2:Q5.41",
            "quoted_wording": "sha256:d3785560fd2f6612ad2b2338c67443c7f77e7c5e0e91d81669536963b98f7aa4"
          },
          "mechanism": "Prior myocardial infarction is a consequence of hypertension and represents target organ damage. Patients with prior MI are prescribed intensive antihypertensive regimens.",
          "justification": "This is a descendant of the outcome (consequence of hypertension severity).",
          "role": "descendant_of_outcome",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        },
        {
          "variable": {
            "kind": "variable",
            "key": "m2:Q5.61",
            "quoted_wording": "sha256:b82f826fbe176b50bfb23894466b23ecfe4403cfea676d696c31e8a43e808747"
          },
          "mechanism": "Prior stroke is a complication of hypertension and indicates hypertension-related organ damage, requiring intensive therapy.",
          "justification": "Descendant outcome marker.",
          "role": "descendant_of_outcome",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        }
      ],
